# Writer boundary of the blob counter and the record conflict and history rows.
# Format: path|function|families|reason
# families: C record conflict (rcf:, rcm:) and field history (rh:, ahq:, ahk:, ahb:) rows · R blob counter and blob queue · - none of these
# One line for each function that the lint finds. The lint fails on a function that is missing,
# on a function that names a family the line does not list, and on a line that no function matches.
# `*` as the function is for the row commit and the blob planner modules only.

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/atom_history/policy.rs|set_field_history_policy|C|writes only a canonical field policy and the logical format fence in one native transaction; no history row or blob counter write

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/metadata_store/idempotency.rs|retire_legacy|-|bounded cleanup inside the reserved idempotency namespace; deletes only validated legacy idem keys and writes its cleanup marker in the native request snapshot; no tip, atom or counter keys

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/delete_replay.rs|raise_replay_cutoff|-|explicit stopped-home maintenance (`lastdb db recount --delete-cutoff`): puts the one replay cutoff row; no record, history, blob counter or conflict row

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/counter/commit.rs|*|C|the row commit: releases rcf: conflict rows, writes queue and blob planner rows and guarded deletes in one batch_mutate that joins the pending batch of the request
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/blob_counter/commit.rs|*|R|the blob planner: blob counters and queue entries change in the batch of the record write (records.rs), or in the request scope of a blob row put
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/blob_counter/dwell_chunk.rs|*|R|the dwell chunk: reads the counter again in the write gate, then deletes the blob row, the counter and the queue entry in one batch (the retirement of a bucket is the guarded delete of the planner)
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/blob_counter/recount.rs|*|R|the blob step of the offline recount: writes the exact blob counters and deletes stale queue entries on a stopped home, in whole batches

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/keep_small.rs|clear_keep_small_distrust_marker|-|keep-small meter distrust marker
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/keep_small.rs|note_keep_small_hydrate_failure|-|keep-small meter distrust marker

# db_catalog_store.rs::drop_scoped_source_rows deletes every row of one scope through a store argument (records, history rows and blob counters go together). The lint cannot see keys that a caller hands to it.

fold_db/crates/core/src/storage/encrypting_store/kv_store_impl.rs|restore_batch_put|C R|store layer: passes a restored row to the inner store

fold_db/crates/core/src/storage/traits/kv.rs|restore_batch_put|C R|store trait: default restore of one row

lastdb_node/src/bin/received_range_seed.rs|activate_generated_receivers|-|CI-only generated share_subscriptions controls in an isolated owned home; mutation manager owns all tip, atom, and counter writes
lastdb_node/src/bin/received_range_seed.rs|activate_generated_send_rule|-|CI-only generated share_rules control for the send check in an isolated owned home; mutation manager owns all tip, atom, record, and counter writes

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/erase_meters.rs|record_atom_delete_audit|-|final dellog audit facts only, optionally database-prefixed; staged in the same native batch as the erase, with no atom, tip, or counter keys
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/counter/restore_validation.rs|finish|-|exclusive restore completion deletes only its durable pending marker after exact read-only counter verification

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/record_conflicts/purge.rs|purged_record_conflicts|C|builds the deletes of the rcf: rows, their queue entries and the rcm: marker of purged records; the caller puts them in the purge batch
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/records.rs|stage_records|-|format 7 home: puts rk: record values, their ak: entry changes, the rh: field history copies with their ahq: queue and ahk: count rows, and the blob planner rows of blob_counter_mutations in one native batch; creates no atom, field tip, archive row or atom counter
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/atom_history/records.rs|commit_history_release|-|format 7 home: releases rh: field history copies with their ahq: queue entries, ahk: count rows and the blob planner rows of blob_counter_mutations in one native batch; no tip, atom, archive row or atom counter
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/atom_history/release.rs|release_dropped_history|-|format 7 schema drop: releases the rh: field history copies of a dropped schema with their ahq: queue entries, deletes their ahk: count rows and writes the blob planner rows of blob_counter_mutations in one native batch, inside the write scope of one release batch; no tip, atom, archive row or atom counter
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/record_store/schema_release.rs|release_batch|-|format 7 schema drop: in one write scope, reads one bounded batch of the rk: records or ak: entries of a dropped schema again by key and deletes them, with the rcf:/rcm: deletes of purged_record_conflicts and the blob planner rows of blob_counter_mutations, in one native batch
# Conversion coverage lives in its own namespace, never the atom store.
